            <register>
               <name>HFXTDYN</name>
               <description>Alternative target values for HFXT configuration

Software can change these values to dynamically transition the HFXT configuration while HFXT is running.
Set SEL to select the alternative set of target values.</description>
               <addressOffset>288</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x14464b6d</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>SEL</name>
                     <description>Select the dynamic configuration.

Amplitude ramping will always happen using the values in HFXTINIT, and HFXTTARG.
Afterwards, this bit can be used to select between HFXTTARG and HFXTDYN.
Hardware will ensure a smooth transition of analog control signals.</description>
                     <bitRange>[31:31]</bitRange>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DYNAMIC</name>
                           <value>0x1</value>
                           <description>Select configuration in CKM.HFXTDYN0 and CKM.HFXTDYN1.</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>TARGET</name>
                           <value>0x0</value>
                           <description>Select configuration in CKM.HFXTTARG0 and CKM.HFXTTARG1.</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>AMPTHR</name>
                     <description>Minimum HFXT amplitude</description>
                     <bitRange>[29:23]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
