            </register>
            <register>
               <name>AMPCFG0</name>
               <description>Amplitude Compensation Configuration 0</description>
               <addressOffset>292</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x003f8882</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>Q2DLY</name>
                     <description>Q2CAP change delay.

Number of clock cycles to wait before changing Q2CAP by one step.
Clock frequency defined in FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[31:28]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>Q1DLY</name>
                     <description>Q1CAP change delay.

Number of clock cycles to wait before changing Q1CAP by one step.
Clock frequency defined in FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[27:24]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>ADCDLY</name>
                     <description>ADC and PEAKDET startup time.

Number of clock cycles to wait after enabling the PEAKDET and ADC before the first measurement.
Clock frequency defined in FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[23:20]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>LDOSTART</name>
                     <description>LDO startup time.

Number of clock cycles to bypass the LDO resistors for faster startup.
Clock frequency defined in FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[19:15]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>INJWAIT</name>
                     <description>Inject HFOSC for faster HFXT startup.

This value specifies the number of clock cycles to wait after injection is done.
The clock speed is defined in FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[14:10]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>INJTIME</name>
                     <description>Inject HFOSC for faster HFXT startup.

This value specifies the number of clock cycles the injection is enabled.
The clock speed is defined in FSMRATE.
Set to 0 to disable injection.</description>
                     <bitRange>[9:5]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>FSMRATE</name>
                     <description>Update rate for the AMPCOMP update rate.
Also affects the clock rate for the Amplitude ADC.

The update rate is 6MHz / (FSMRATE+1).</description>
                     <bitRange>[4:0]</bitRange>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>_250K</name>
                           <value>0x17</value>
                           <description>250 kHz</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>_500K</name>
                           <value>0xb</value>
                           <description>500 kHz</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>_1M</name>
                           <value>0x5</value>
                           <description>1 MHz</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>_2M</name>
                           <value>0x2</value>
                           <description>2 MHz</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>_3M</name>
                           <value>0x1</value>
                           <description>3 MHz</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>_6M</name>
                           <value>0x0</value>
                           <description>6 MHz</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>AMPCFG1</name>
               <description>Amplitude Compensation Configuration 1</description>
               <addressOffset>296</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x260ff0ff</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>IDACDLY</name>
                     <description>IDAC change delay.

Time to wait before changing IDAC by one step.
This time needs to be long enough for the crystal to settle.
The number of clock cycles to wait is IDACDLY$lt;$lt;4 + 15.
Clock frequency defined in AMPCFG0.FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[31:28]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>IREFDLY</name>
                     <description>IREF change delay.

Number of clock cycles to wait before changing IREF by one step.
Clock frequency defined in AMPCFG0.FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[27:24]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>BIASLT</name>
                     <description>Lifetime of the amplitude ADC bias value.
This value specifies the number of adjustment intervals,
until the ADC bias value has to be measured again.
Set to 0 to disable automatic bias measurements.</description>
                     <bitRange>[23:12]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>INTERVAL</name>
                     <description>Interval for amplitude adjustments.
Set to 0 to disable periodic adjustments.

This value specifies the number of clock cycles between adjustments.
The clock speed is defined in AMPCFG0.FSMRATE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[11:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>LOOPCFG</name>
               <description>Configuration Register for the Tracking Loop</description>
               <addressOffset>300</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x605e4fb2</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>FINETRIM_INIT</name>
                     <description>Initial value for the resistor fine trim</description>
                     <bitRange>[31:26]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>BOOST_TARGET</name>
                     <description>Error-updates for 4xBOOST_TARGET times using KI_BOOST/KP_BOOST, before using KI/KP.
Note: If boost is used for long duration using large values of KI_BOOST $amp; KP_BOOST, the oscillator frequency can reach well above the max frequence limit of the design, causing unexpected behaviour.</description>
                     <bitRange>[25:21]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>KP_BOOST</name>
                     <description>Proportional loop coefficient during BOOST</description>
                     <bitRange>[20:18]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>KI_BOOST</name>
                     <description>Integral loop coefficient during BOOST</description>
                     <bitRange>[17:15]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>SETTLED_TARGET</name>
                     <description>Number of HFOSC tracking loop updates before HFOSC is considered &#34;settled&#34;. The tracking loop updates at a rough frequency of (2*Reference frequency/256).
If the reference frequency is 48MHz, the loop update frequency comes out to be 375Khz.
Internally the MMR is multiplied by 4</description>
                     <bitRange>[14:10]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>OOR_LIMIT</name>
                     <description>Out-of-range threshold. OOR_LIMIT is compared with absolute value of 5 MSB bits of loop filter error.</description>
                     <bitRange>[9:6]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>KP</name>
                     <description>Proportional loop coefficient</description>
                     <bitRange>[5:3]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>KI</name>
                     <description>Integral loop coefficient</description>
                     <bitRange>[2:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>LOOPCFG1</name>
               <description>Configuration Register for underclocking HFOSC</description>
               <addressOffset>304</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x0000003f</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>SETTLEIRQ</name>
                     <description>Configuration to enable the interrupt when the HFOSC tracking loop has settled. The interrupt will be based on LOOPCFG.SETTLED_TARGET.</description>
                     <bitRange>[25:25]</bitRange>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>ENABLE</name>
                           <value>0x1</value>
                           <description>Enable the interrupt to indicate that HFOSC tracking loop has settled.</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DISABLE</name>
                           <value>0x0</value>
                           <description>Disable the interrupt to indicate that HFOSC tracking loop has settled.</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>UNDERCLKCNT</name>
                     <description>Timer to trigger HFOSC underclocking. The timer will run at approximately 32.768 KHz.</description>
                     <bitRange>[24:6]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>KIOFF</name>
                     <description>Based on HFTRACKCTRL.UNDERCLK configuration, after an event is triggerred, KI of the HFOSC tracking loop will be reduced by this amount.</description>
                     <bitRange>[5:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>AFOSCCTL</name>
               <description>Audio frequency oscillator control</description>
               <addressOffset>320</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>PW</name>
                     <description>Password protection for QUALBYP.

Write this field to 0xA5 to accept writes to QUALBYP.</description>
                     <bitRange>[31:24]</bitRange>
                     <access>write-only</access>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>AUTODIS</name>
                     <description>If set, AFOSC can be disabled by PMCTL upon standby entry. EN bit will be overriden with a value 0 and user has to manually re-enable AFOSC.</description>
                     <bitRange>[2:2]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>QUALBYP</name>
                     <description>Clock qualification bypass.

AFOSC qualification will skip a fixed number of clock cycles to prevent glitches 
or frequency overshoots from reaching the system. Setting this bit will bypass the qualification.
This bit can be locked in SYS0. If unlocked, it is password protected with PW.</description>
                     <bitRange>[1:1]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>EN</name>
                     <description>Enable AFOSC.</description>
                     <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>AFTRACKCTL</name>
