            </register>
            <register>
               <name>TRIGCNT</name>
               <description>Trigger Counter

Stop-counter control and status.</description>
               <addressOffset>532</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>CNT</name>
                     <description>Number of stop events to ignore when [TDC.TRIGCNTCFG.EN] is 1.

Read CNT to get the remaining number of stop events to ignore during a TDC measurement.  

Write CNT to update the remaining number of stop events to ignore during a TDC measurement. The TDC measurement ignores updates of CNT if there are no more stop events left to ignore.

When [TDC.TRIGCNTCFG.EN] is 1, [TDC.TRIGCNTLOAD.CNT] is loaded into CNT at the start of the measurement. </description>
                     <bitRange>[15:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>TRIGCNTLOAD</name>
               <description>Trigger Counter Load

Stop-counter load.</description>
               <addressOffset>536</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>CNT</name>
                     <description>Number of stop events to ignore when [TDC.TRIGCNTCFG.EN] is 1.

To measure frequency of an event source: 
- Set start event equal to stop event.
- Set CNT to number of periods to measure. Both 0 and 1 values measures a single event source period.

To measure pulse width of an event source:
- Set start event source equal to stop event source.
- Select different polarity for start and stop event.
- Set CNT to 0.

To measure time from the start event to the Nth stop event when N $gt; 1:
- Select different start and stop event source.
- Set CNT to (N-1). 

See the Technical Reference Manual for event timing requirements. 

When [TDC.TRIGCNTCFG.EN] is 1, CNT is loaded into [TDC.TRIGCNT.CNT] at the start of the measurement.
</description>
                     <bitRange>[15:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>TRIGCNTCFG</name>
               <description>Trigger Counter Configuration

Stop-counter configuration.</description>
               <addressOffset>540</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>EN</name>
                     <description>Enable stop-counter.

0: Disable stop-counter.
1: Enable stop-counter.

Change only while [TDC.STAT.STATE] is IDLE.</description>
                     <bitRange>[0:0]</bitRange>
                  </field>
               </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
               <name>PRECTL</name>
               <description>Prescaler Control

The prescaler can be used to count events that are faster than the bus rate. 
It can be used to:
- count pulses on a specified event from the asynchronous event bus.
- prescale a specified event from the asynchronous event bus. 

To use the prescaler output as an event source in TDC measurements you must set both TRIGSRC.START_SRC and TRIGSRC.STOP_SRC to TDC_PRE.

It is recommended to use the prescaler when the signal frequency to measure exceeds 1/10th of the bus rate.</description>
               <addressOffset>544</addressOffset>
               <access>read-write</access>
               <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
               <fields>
                  <field>
                     <name>RESET_N</name>
                     <description>Prescaler reset.

0: Reset prescaler.
1: Release reset of prescaler.

AUX_TDC_PRE event becomes 0 when you reset the prescaler. </description>
                     <bitRange>[7:7]</bitRange>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>RATIO</name>
                     <description>Prescaler ratio. 

This controls how often the TDC_PRE event is generated by the prescaler. </description>
                     <bitRange>[6:6]</bitRange>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DIV64</name>
                           <value>0x1</value>
                           <description>Prescaler divides input by 64. 

AUX_TDC_PRE event has a rising edge for every 64 rising edges of the input. AUX_TDC_PRE event toggles on every 32nd rising edge of the input. </description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DIV16</name>
                           <value>0x0</value>
                           <description>Prescaler divides input by 16. 

AUX_TDC_PRE event has a rising edge for every 16 rising edges of the input. AUX_TDC_PRE event toggles on every 8th rising edge of the input. </description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                     </enumeratedValues>
                  </field>
                  <field>
                     <name>SRC</name>
                     <description>Prescaler event source. 

Select an event from the asynchronous AUX event bus to connect to the prescaler input. 

Configure only while RESET_N is 0.</description>
                     <bitRange>[4:0]</bitRange>
                     <enumeratedValues>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>AFOSC</name>
                           <value>0x17</value>
                           <description>Audio frequency on-chip oscillator</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>HFXT</name>
                           <value>0x16</value>
                           <description>High frequency crystal oscillator</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>HFOSC</name>
                           <value>0x15</value>
                           <description>High frequency on-chip oscillator</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB15</name>
                           <value>0x14</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 15</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB14</name>
                           <value>0x13</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 14</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB13</name>
                           <value>0x12</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 13</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB12</name>
                           <value>0x11</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 12</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB11</name>
                           <value>0x10</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 11</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB10</name>
                           <value>0xf</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 10</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB9</name>
                           <value>0xe</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 9</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB8</name>
                           <value>0xd</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 8</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB7</name>
                           <value>0xc</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 7</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB6</name>
                           <value>0xb</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 6</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB5</name>
                           <value>0xa</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 5</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB4</name>
                           <value>0x9</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 4</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB3</name>
                           <value>0x8</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 3</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB2</name>
                           <value>0x7</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 2</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB1</name>
                           <value>0x6</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 1</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>DTB0</name>
                           <value>0x5</value>
                           <description>Digital testbus bit 0</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>GPI</name>
                           <value>0x4</value>
                           <description>General purpose input signal</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>LFCLK_DLY</name>
                           <value>0x3</value>
                           <description>Delayed version of selected LFCLK</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>LFXT</name>
                           <value>0x2</value>
                           <description>Low frequency crystal oscillator</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>LFOSC</name>
                           <value>0x1</value>
                           <description>Low frequency on-chip oscillator</description>
                        </enumeratedValue>
                        <enumeratedValue>
                           <name>LFTICK</name>
